1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:05,930
Aaaaah!

2
00:00:06,013 --> 00:00:06,843
It's Rob Luffy!

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,320
Then it's true.

4
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,977
They came here to kill Vegapunk
just as he feared that they would.

5
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,137
Who the hell invited you pigeon guy?

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,396
You get out of here!

7
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,640
This is a government island.

8
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,257
Oh, crap, you're right.

9
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:24,397
We're the ones who aren't
supposed to be here.

10
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,310
Ah!

11
00:00:25,393 --> 00:00:26,223
Will you focus?

12
00:00:26,306 --> 00:00:27,136
None of that matters!

13
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:28,500
Come on, Luffy.

14
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:30,577
We've got to get to the upper level now.

15
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:31,920
The Straw Hats, huh?

16
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,931
Didn't know this place had a pest problem.

17
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,360
Jewelry Bonnie, too.

18
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:39,340
But we can't do anything yet, Luchi.

19
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,517
Remember, Straw Hat is an
emperor of the sea now.

20
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,177
We can't fight him without
permission from the top.

21
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:46,090
He's right.

22
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,007
The four emperors often
have powerful allies.

23
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,734
One little scuffle could lead to a war.

24
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,200
Send a report to the Navy now. Roger.

25
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,620
I'm not sure we can
avoid a fight so easily.

26
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:04,100
I gotta go, Jinbei. Hold on to you.

27
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,131
Huffy, what's the matter?

28
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,060
What happened?

29
00:01:18,180 --> 00:01:19,440
Wait, I know her.

30
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:21,860
It's that girl from before.

31
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:24,060
Chopper, help her, please.

32
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:29,260
I'm sorry, though.

33
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:32,540
I think this is more
Frankie's specialty than mine.

34
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:42,520
This is government business.

35
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:44,998
You would be wise to stay out of it.

36
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:48,420
She fed us!

37
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:52,501
She took care of us when we came
here, and that makes her a friend!

38
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:25,030
Oh...

39
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:29,780
Bunchy, Bunchy Notimate, I got one piece!

40
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:41,260
I can't sleep, and the brain is біль.

41
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,557
And I will fight!

42
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:49,620
gewalm All Over's is the
adventure of this adventure.

43
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,540
The Straw Hats are on Egghead?

44
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,860
Why, dammit?

45
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,697
See this?

46
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:40,604
You give people an inch and they
give you nothing but a headache.

47
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:44,077
You must have figured out that
CP0 was there to kill him.

48
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,237
That's not a good sign.

49
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,220
Yes, sir.

50
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:49,911
That's likely why they had to
use Espar to teleport inside.

51
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:53,580
What they did is declare war.

52
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,698
Wish they'd had the common
sense to contact me first.

53
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,340
Those arrogant brats.

54
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:04,037
If Vegapunk has the Straw Hats on his
side, this could be a real disaster.

55
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:06,826
Who knows how many good
marines we could lose.

56
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:09,480
Where's Kizaru?

57
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,137
He's on his way to Egghead right now.

58
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:15,691
He was already en route, in
service of a different mission.

59
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:20,620
Tell Luchi to avoid any further
action until backup arrives. Sir!

60
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:25,340
No matter what happens, we
cannot let him fight Straw Hat!

61
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,340
Intruder alert!

62
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,035
Evacuate immediately!

63
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:33,100
I repeat, evacuate immediately!

64
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,480
You take Bonnie, I'll take her. Let's go!

65
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,645
Yeah, we need to get her
to Franky right away!

66
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,220
You ready, Luffy?

67
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:49,340
Go on without me. Woo-hoo!

68
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,400
Oh, my God.

69
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:02,072
What was that form in your wanted poster?

70
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,391
What, you want to see it?

71
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,160
Do you need to ask?

72
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,080
Ha!

73
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,000
What the hell?

74
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,660
Oh, my God.

75
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:44,440
I'll be damned.

76
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:46,457
This should be fun.

77
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:52,590
Oh,

78
00:07:52,673 --> 00:07:53,503
he he

79
00:07:53,586 --> 00:07:59,960
he

80
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:17,210
he he!

81
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:21,040
Hey! Yoo-hoo! Pigeon guy!

82
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,580
Get over here!

83
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:24,140
Let's fight some more!

84
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:34,014
Still playing games, even
when your life is on the line?

85
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,980
I'm starting to get annoyed.

86
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,350
Ah, no!

87
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,630
Ah!

88
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:10,140
Don't get cocky, Straw Hat.

89
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:13,140
I've gotten stronger just like you have.

90
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:15,891
All the better to eat prey like you alive.

91
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,037
Wait, something's different.

92
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:23,649
He definitely didn't
look like that before.

93
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:26,040
Stop, Luchi!

94
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:28,476
We don't have authorization for this!

95
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,060
His speed is incredible,
but so is his control.

96
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:40,638
It's rare that an awakened Snow user
can maintain their state of mind.

97
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,350
What? Oh!

98
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:52,910
Oh!

99
00:09:52,993 --> 00:09:54,020
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

100
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:55,410
Oh!

101
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:58,290
Oh!

102
00:09:58,373 --> 00:09:59,203
He-he-he-he!

103
00:09:59,286 --> 00:10:00,116
It's mine!

104
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,840
Susie! Susie! Susie!

105
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:13,790
You're out of control!

106
00:10:13,873 --> 00:10:15,717
Please think of the position you're in!

107
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:18,329
The government will
hunt you down for this!

108
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,070
Shaka!

109
00:10:28,153 --> 00:10:28,983
What happened?

110
00:10:29,066 --> 00:10:30,677
Did the Whitehead Warrior appear?

111
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,590
Oh, my God!

112
00:10:31,673 --> 00:10:32,503
Real Vegapunk!

113
00:10:32,586 --> 00:10:34,873
How the hell did he get up here so fast?

114
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,790
Remarkable!

115
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,160
Tell me more!

116
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,837
I must know everything
about this transformation!

117
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,440
What is that for?

118
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,137
Well, it's new, so we
don't know much either.

119
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,102
But it's a Gum-Gum thing, right?

120
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:54,202
It's a Devil Fruit encyclopedia.

121
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:57,154
There is no mention of a Gum-Gum fruit.

122
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:59,080
This must be something else.

123
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:00,430
Huh?

124
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,337
Wait, are you saying it's
a different Devil Fruit?

125
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:06,717
If that's true, then why does
he say Gum-Gum all the time?

126
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:11,720
Oh, he's so beautiful.

127
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:16,214
That is a figure from the ancient past,

128
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:19,900
one with the same form
your captain has now.

129
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,900
A god from the old texts.

130
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:25,500
A god?

131
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,140
I'm sorry, Luffy?

132
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:28,949
Stupid and cornered Luffy?

133
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:31,090
Yes.

134
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,637
The warrior of liberation.

135
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:38,580
He who plays the fool
and brings smiles to all.

136
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:41,700
There's no mistaking him.

137
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,760
He is the sun god, Nika!

138
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:48,950
Nika?

139
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:50,592
I've never heard of him.

140
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:51,917
That's no surprise.

141
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,941
The world government erased
his name from history.

142
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:58,837
But as long as people yearn
for the warrior of liberation,

143
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,797
he will never truly disappear.

144
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:05,060
For it is desire that brings
forth everything in this world.

145
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:09,460
Take for example, the devil
fruits and all their power.

146
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,480
You can see it, can't you?

147
00:12:14,380 --> 00:12:19,040
Each Devil Fruit is a possibility
for evolution that someone desires.

148
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,900
I wish I could do this.

149
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:22,520
I wish I could do that.

150
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:26,237
All of the powers represent
potential futures of humanity.

151
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:31,260
But these fantastic possibilities
are not a natural part of this world.

152
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:35,420
So the mother of nature,
the sea, rejects them.

153
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:39,420
Therefore, you might say...

154
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:47,160
Those who have powers live
in different realities.

155
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:50,980
Realities someone dreamed of.

156
00:12:56,320 --> 00:12:58,040
That is my hypothesis!

157
00:12:59,720 --> 00:13:03,060
Wonder God's existence is irrelevant!

158
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:07,320
What an interesting
world, wouldn't you say?

159
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:15,457
Do those idiots know
where they're fighting?

160
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:17,160
This isn't a playground.

161
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:20,400
Not for pirates and not for CP0, either.

162
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:26,120
Why are you bothering me on my day off?

163
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:28,379
Why did you take so long to answer?

164
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,630
Whatever.

165
00:13:29,713 --> 00:13:30,618
I'm here, aren't I?

166
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,331
So what's the plan, punk?

167
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:36,567
Cipher Pole is our ally, and the
pirates are the enemy, right?

168
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:39,840
Do you want me to just
back up CP0 or what?

169
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:42,364
Quite the opposite, I'm afraid.

170
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:47,208
CP0 is here to assassinate me,
so I need your help to escape.

171
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:50,037
Don't get caught up in the details.

172
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,217
Just keep them away.

173
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,300
I can't do that.

174
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,676
Do you know what they do to traitors?

175
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,220
You're right.

176
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,540
My apologies.

177
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,412
But let me ask you this.

178
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:01,410
Sentomaru?

179
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:04,520
Can't you do this one teensy favor for me?

180
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:08,020
The man who saved you from poverty?

181
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:10,440
All those years ago?

182
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:13,800
Wow, no pressure, huh?

183
00:14:21,780 --> 00:14:23,960
Is he going to attack us?

184
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:26,840
Three Seraphim.

185
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,660
I'm not looking forward to this.

186
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,764
Esbear, thin out their numbers.

187
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:37,000
Esbear, don't move!

188
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:40,600
We can't beat them. Not like this.

189
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:42,200
Go, Esbear!

190
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,660
Take out CP Zero!

191
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:44,899
They're the enemy!

192
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,010
Retreat!

193
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:03,480
We need a new plan, and fast. No kidding.

194
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:08,537
So the issue is that Central Moria outranks
the authority chips we're carrying?

195
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:09,450
That's right.

196
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:11,816
The system of control is a hierarchy.

197
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,017
If someone whose higher
rank gives an order,

198
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,377
that's the order the Seraphim will follow.

199
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:19,695
The highest on the authority
chain are the five elders.

200
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,380
The second highest is Dr.

201
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:25,370
Vegapunk

202
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:28,220
The third is Saint Moria.

203
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:33,061
And authority chip holders
like us are the fourth!

204
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:38,600
No matter what we do, Saint Maru's
commands will always be prioritized.

205
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:43,177
Then why don't we make a call to the
five elders and have them take control?

206
00:15:43,260 --> 00:15:44,731
It doesn't work that way!

207
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:48,117
Pacifistas have to receive
their commands directly.

208
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:52,940
They won't react to a transponder snail,
even if it is the Five Elders Calling.

209
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:57,022
Then what are we supposed to do?

210
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,357
The Seraphim are valuable
government property.

211
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:00,857
We can't just destroy them.

212
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:01,900
Darn it, Lucci!

213
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,236
You really didn't think this through.

214
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:16,360
Ha ha ha ha!

215
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:17,730
Ha ha ha!

216
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:18,650
Woo hoo!

217
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,060
You ready?

218
00:16:26,320 --> 00:16:27,340
Go, go!

219
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:29,510
Move!

220
00:16:29,820 --> 00:16:30,650
Go!

221
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:37,380
Time to do this.

222
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:41,717
First, F-Snake, guide Straw Hat and
his friends to the vacuum rocket.

223
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:44,271
They need to make it to the frontier dome.

224
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:46,660
S-Hawk! S-Sharp!

225
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:48,400
Hold CP0 back!

226
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:51,964
Chopper, do those children
look familiar to you?

227
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,557
Apart from the Black Wings and the Flames,

228
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:57,257
they all look like former
warlords of the sea.

229
00:16:57,340 --> 00:16:58,170
You're right.

230
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,498
There's no way that's a coincidence.

231
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:03,560
The government must have
made clones out of us.

232
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:06,090
Hey!

233
00:17:06,173 --> 00:17:07,003
Axe Guy!

234
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:12,060
It's been a while, old buddy.

235
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:14,380
Tch, Straw Hat.

236
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:18,157
Current circumstances aside,
you and I are enemies.

237
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:19,480
And I have a name.

238
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:21,210
So what?

239
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:22,677
You're helping Punk escape?

240
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:23,995
Do I have that right?

241
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:25,390
Uh-huh.

242
00:17:25,473 --> 00:17:26,417
I like his apple head.

243
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,330
And he asked.

244
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:30,297
Well, that doesn't exactly
fill me with confidence.

245
00:17:30,380 --> 00:17:32,740
But I suppose you are an emperor now.

246
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:43,780
Hand pistol.

247
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:50,680
Black Sky!

248
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,360
That takes care of your commander.

249
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:58,060
Seraphim, you follow our orders now.

250
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,020
I'm sorry!

251
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:04,620
I just got to do it, now you're dead!

252
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:06,890
Idiot.

253
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,480
You didn't distract me.

254
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,520
I saw that it coming.

255
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:28,120
That was so short.

256
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,100
I'm locked in time.

257
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,200
Hurry up and die.

258
00:18:42,060 --> 00:18:44,920
I can't take control
until you're unconscious.

259
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:29,060
I'm sure you thought you had a fine strategy
on writing our orders to the Seraphim.

260
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:32,300
But all you did was put a
nail in your own carpet!

261
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,440
GUMGUM!

262
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:02,800
GUMGUM! JOHN!

263
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:18,870
Loochie.

264
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:26,800
Now's our chance!

265
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,430
Hurry, Luffy!

266
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,237
If we want to save this girl's life,

267
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:33,197
then we have to get to
Vegapunk's lab immediately!

268
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:37,540
I mean, it's not like I don't
want to, but, uh... Blah!

269
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:47,000
I can't stop spinning!

270
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,560
Whoa, you really can't stop spinning!

271
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:58,457
Somebody call a doctor, quick!

272
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:00,834
Sorry, I can't stop the winner to grow!

273
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:08,380
Factory! Hurry!

274
00:21:37,620 --> 00:21:40,337
Is there nothing we can
do to stop these things?

275
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:42,538
We're losing men to our own weapons.

276
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:46,348
I shudder to imagine how strong
they'll be once they grow up.

277
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:48,640
Hey, Vegapunk!

278
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:51,590
What's wrong?

279
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,979
Tell me the truth.

280
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,520
What is that power?

281
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:57,677
And what the hell is that
Jinbei thing doing with it?

282
00:21:57,760 --> 00:22:00,584
Guess that looks like the
Swim Swim Fruit to me.

283
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:02,317
What's the Swim Swim Fruit?

284
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,240
It's his.

285
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:08,176
My hard-boiled brother from another
mother, Sonar Pink, has that power.

286
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:10,100
I'd recognize it anywhere.

287
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:19,777
But it's impossible for there to
be two of the same Devil Fruit,

288
00:22:19,860 --> 00:22:22,740
so that means my bro must have died!

289
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,600
My poor bro!

290
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,840
So you would think.

291
00:22:29,220 --> 00:22:30,637
But he's not dead.

292
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,920
He's just been held in Impel Down.

293
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:35,480
Hold up.

294
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:39,113
Does that mean you found a
way to duplicate Devil Fruits?

295
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:43,920
Well, some Devil Fruits can be copied.

296
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:50,220
But it only works with Snow types.

297
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:58,560
The less said about Caesar's
smile experiments, the better.

298
00:22:59,360 --> 00:23:01,301
Yeah, he can go straight to hell.

299
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:07,180
The smiles offer a high
risk and low success rate.

300
00:23:07,500 --> 00:23:09,680
They only work one time out of ten.

301
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:13,497
And those who aren't granted power
never stop smiling or laughing.

302
00:23:13,580 --> 00:23:16,217
They can't even mourn for
their lost loved ones.

303
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,960
It's sick. Caesar.

304
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:22,213
Just hearing his name again
makes me want to blow chunks.

305
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:27,711
Aberrations such as those notwithstanding.

306
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:29,977
I have not given up.

307
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:32,780
If we had enough fun to, and enough time,

308
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:36,300
we could replicate any
Devil Fruit in the world.

309
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:40,920
So, I'm not sure if they'll awaken.

310
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:52,137
I've tried to recreate Lock
powers, but I've had no luck.

311
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:56,840
And yet, for a Paramecia fruit,

312
00:23:57,080 --> 00:24:00,137
I need only acquire the
bloodline elements of its owner.

313
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:03,017
Then I can synthesize a special compound!

314
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:07,700
Which, when administered, confers the
Devil Fruit power to another person.

315
00:24:13,240 --> 00:24:17,358
Observe, that's the fluid you see
flowing through the seraphim's arms.

316
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:20,080
The green blood.

317
00:24:22,560 --> 00:24:23,780
Hold up!

318
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:25,687
You made a new can of blood?

319
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:30,140
L-love?

320
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:33,260
Beam!

321
00:24:41,220 --> 00:24:47,080
I believe that Seraphic represents the
pinnacle of modern scientific possibility.

322
00:24:51,100 --> 00:24:52,880
Where's the shock go?

323
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:02,600
Do you know what's that make them?

324
00:25:03,580 --> 00:25:06,780
The strongest form of humanity in history.

325
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:10,057
Is that why the government
got rid of them?

326
00:25:10,140 --> 00:25:15,022
Why the hell would you even make something
stronger than a warlord, you psychopath?

327
00:25:15,140 --> 00:25:17,860
They're navy weapons killing machines.

328
00:25:18,420 --> 00:25:19,250
Yes.

329
00:25:19,333 --> 00:25:21,846
And sooner or later,
they'll be aiming for us.

330
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,340
Hold on, Sentomaru!

331
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:37,140
Stay back!

332
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:40,400
This isn't over yet.

333
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:55,440
Sentomaru, please stay safe!

334
00:25:57,280 --> 00:26:00,398
Now where did that little
friend of yours run off to?

335
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:02,240
I don't know.

336
00:26:02,860 --> 00:26:04,400
And he's not my friend!

337
00:26:05,020 --> 00:26:06,040
What a shame.

338
00:26:06,400 --> 00:26:08,282
Guess you're all alone, traitor.

339
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,320
We're out.

340
00:26:33,980 --> 00:26:34,810
Hey! Hey!

341
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:40,020
You, boy!

342
00:26:41,740 --> 00:26:42,570
Uuh! You, boy!

343
00:26:42,653 --> 00:26:43,560
You, boy!

344
00:26:47,560 --> 00:26:48,390
You, boy!

345
00:26:48,473 --> 00:26:49,303
Ah!

346
00:26:49,386 --> 00:26:50,216
Oh!

347
00:26:50,540 --> 00:26:51,370
Oh! Ahh!

348
00:26:52,200 --> 00:26:53,300
Oh!

349
00:26:53,860 --> 00:26:54,690
Yes, I'm!

350
00:26:59,720 --> 00:27:00,820
Ah!

351
00:27:02,860 --> 00:27:03,960
Ah!

352
00:27:07,140 --> 00:27:07,970
Huh?

353
00:27:08,660 --> 00:27:09,490
Hmm?

354
00:27:10,220 --> 00:27:11,050
You?

355
00:27:11,133 --> 00:27:11,963
Who? Huh?

356
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:13,130
Huh?

357
00:27:13,980 --> 00:27:14,810
Huh? Huh?

358
00:27:16,080 --> 00:27:17,170
Uh? Ah...

359
00:27:23,470 --> 00:27:24,990
Huh... Huh...

360
00:27:25,490 --> 00:27:26,650
Uh...

361
00:27:30,330 --> 00:27:32,470
Ah! Ah!

362
00:27:32,810 --> 00:27:35,130
Hehehehe... Uh! Uh!

363
00:27:36,670 --> 00:27:37,830
Ah!

364
00:27:38,550 --> 00:27:39,380
Uh!

365
00:27:39,630 --> 00:27:40,530
Ah!

366
00:27:45,270 --> 00:27:46,347
Ha!

367
00:27:46,430 --> 00:27:47,330
Mm-hmm.

368
00:27:54,390 --> 00:27:56,450
Don't stop!

369
00:28:06,530 --> 00:28:07,360
God!

370
00:28:07,443 --> 00:28:08,273
Come on!

371
00:28:15,830 --> 00:28:16,660
Rocky!

372
00:28:21,710 --> 00:28:23,357
When did he get so powerful?

373
00:28:26,850 --> 00:28:27,680
Damn it.

374
00:28:31,090 --> 00:28:32,561
I'm losing consciousness.

375
00:28:37,030 --> 00:28:37,860
Ha-ha-ha!

376
00:28:44,630 --> 00:28:46,250
Follow me, quickly!

377
00:28:56,850 --> 00:28:58,330
I said hurry!

378
00:29:00,850 --> 00:29:03,909
This is no time to be
dragging your feet, you fools!

379
00:29:05,030 --> 00:29:06,971
The vacuum rocket is right there!

380
00:29:07,750 --> 00:29:09,110
Now get on!

381
00:29:10,210 --> 00:29:11,330
Why, thank you!

382
00:29:11,590 --> 00:29:14,531
You know you're much kinder
than the real Hancock.

383
00:29:14,930 --> 00:29:17,090
We owe you one! Much obliged!

384
00:29:17,650 --> 00:29:18,480
What?

385
00:29:18,563 --> 00:29:19,393
Dude, don't be absurd!

386
00:29:19,630 --> 00:29:21,930
I'm just following orders, all right?

387
00:29:27,230 --> 00:29:29,810
Vacuum rocket departing in one minute.

388
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:32,488
Oh wait, come on, we're out of time!

389
00:29:32,790 --> 00:29:34,150
Hurry up!

390
00:29:38,030 --> 00:29:40,570
What do I do? Attention.

391
00:29:40,870 --> 00:29:44,790
Please take caution while
boarding the rocket. Strike!

392
00:29:46,970 --> 00:29:47,800
Go!

393
00:29:48,170 --> 00:29:49,730
Then take care of punk!

394
00:29:50,090 --> 00:29:50,930
You hear me?

395
00:29:53,530 --> 00:29:54,360
Okay!

396
00:29:54,770 --> 00:29:55,652
Leave it to me!

397
00:29:58,070 --> 00:29:58,900
No!

398
00:29:59,130 --> 00:30:00,718
You're going the wrong way!

399
00:30:03,090 --> 00:30:03,920
Caution.

400
00:30:04,070 --> 00:30:06,330
Doors closing in ten seconds.

401
00:30:17,390 --> 00:30:19,510
We're gonna get him off this island.

402
00:30:21,430 --> 00:30:22,807
No matter what!

403
00:30:22,890 --> 00:30:23,910
I promise.

404
00:30:35,350 --> 00:30:36,630
Doors closing.

405
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:44,630
Prepare to launch!

406
00:30:50,410 --> 00:30:51,770
Isn't so neat?

407
00:30:59,710 --> 00:31:02,030
It's certainly something, all right.

408
00:31:02,930 --> 00:31:04,010
Where am I?

409
00:31:04,250 --> 00:31:05,956
What happened to Bagel Punks?

410
00:31:06,630 --> 00:31:07,460
Huh?

411
00:31:08,490 --> 00:31:09,850
Where's Pinchin' Guy?

412
00:31:10,110 --> 00:31:11,830
Let me out of here! Whoa!

413
00:31:12,030 --> 00:31:13,087
Who the hell is this?

414
00:31:13,170 --> 00:31:14,000
It's Loopy!

415
00:31:14,083 --> 00:31:14,913
He's just tired!

416
00:31:14,996 --> 00:31:16,427
I'll give you the details later!

417
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:18,098
How long have I passed out?

418
00:31:19,430 --> 00:31:21,390
Okay, maybe I'll get used to it!

419
00:31:21,850 --> 00:31:23,730
Oh, Gunnar, please shut up!

420
00:31:23,850 --> 00:31:25,030
Easy does it!

421
00:31:25,130 --> 00:31:26,767
You'll shut up too, Grandpa!

422
00:31:26,850 --> 00:31:28,497
Don't get to normal already!

423
00:31:31,510 --> 00:31:32,990
Departing Fabrio base.

424
00:31:34,070 --> 00:31:35,530
Entering Lobby base.

425
00:31:39,610 --> 00:31:43,407
Transit duration 32 seconds.

426
00:31:43,490 --> 00:31:47,027
You have arrived already.

427
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:50,207
All subsequent rockets are cancelled.

428
00:31:50,290 --> 00:31:52,187
Lobby phase under Loguetown.

429
00:31:52,270 --> 00:31:54,670
Frontier dome security system engaged.

430
00:31:55,730 --> 00:31:57,547
Hostile intruder alert.

431
00:31:57,630 --> 00:32:03,810
All researchers evacuate to the factory
immediately and seal all entry points.

432
00:32:10,690 --> 00:32:12,690
Well, I will say this for the man.

433
00:32:14,950 --> 00:32:17,570
He was a faithful bodyguard to Vegapunk.

434
00:32:18,690 --> 00:32:20,330
Tilt his dying breath.

435
00:32:20,950 --> 00:32:22,050
Such a waste.

436
00:32:22,810 --> 00:32:25,163
Didn't have to end like this, Sentomaru.

437
00:32:25,250 --> 00:32:29,267
Need I remind you, our orders are to
wait for the Navy before making a move.

438
00:32:29,350 --> 00:32:31,447
They can twiddle their
thumbs all they like,

439
00:32:31,530 --> 00:32:33,883
but I won't wait for Vegapunk to escape.

440
00:32:34,810 --> 00:32:37,407
What do they even stand
to gain from killing you?

441
00:32:37,490 --> 00:32:40,107
You're the smartest man in the
world, and you're on their side.

442
00:32:40,190 --> 00:32:42,970
If they do this, it'll
be a huge loss for them.

443
00:32:43,530 --> 00:32:44,630
Well, I think so.

444
00:32:44,810 --> 00:32:48,575
But it appears that the higher-ups
have a different perspective.

445
00:32:49,890 --> 00:32:54,327
I certainly made inventions that have
been beneficial to the world government.

446
00:32:54,410 --> 00:32:57,950
Innovations in navigation
technology using sea brism stones.

447
00:32:58,410 --> 00:33:00,110
Cyborg animal modifications.

448
00:33:01,450 --> 00:33:05,607
Not to mention my research on devil
fruits that's unlocked their secrets,

449
00:33:05,690 --> 00:33:08,749
or my creation of human
weapons with the pacifistas.

450
00:33:09,730 --> 00:33:13,190
And now, I've completed
the Seraphim as well.

451
00:33:14,230 --> 00:33:18,887
Now imagine if you thought I might turn
that frightful intelligence against you.

452
00:33:18,970 --> 00:33:20,210
Fuck what you do!

453
00:33:20,510 --> 00:33:23,890
In that case, there's no choice. Hmm?

454
00:33:25,350 --> 00:33:26,180
I said!

455
00:33:26,263 --> 00:33:27,350
I will not!

456
00:33:27,470 --> 00:33:29,467
For the record, I never planned to revolt.

457
00:33:29,550 --> 00:33:32,079
I still need my research
funding after all.

458
00:33:32,450 --> 00:33:36,190
But the powers that be decided
I was troubling that was that.

459
00:33:36,930 --> 00:33:38,577
Alas, life gives you lemons.

460
00:33:38,710 --> 00:33:40,287
Government tries to kill you for them.

461
00:33:40,370 --> 00:33:43,027
That is not how the expression
goes, and you know it!

462
00:33:43,110 --> 00:33:47,581
Just when I faced this quandary, an
emperor and his crew appeared before me.

463
00:33:47,850 --> 00:33:50,321
Fate brought us together, don't you think?

464
00:33:51,270 --> 00:33:52,100
Hold it!

465
00:33:52,183 --> 00:33:53,627
You mean you want to join our crew?

466
00:33:53,710 --> 00:33:55,470
Welcome aboard, crewmates!

467
00:33:56,130 --> 00:33:56,960
Super! Super!

468
00:33:58,330 --> 00:34:00,887
Which of my babies do
you want to see first?

469
00:34:00,970 --> 00:34:02,090
The Sonny?

470
00:34:02,550 --> 00:34:03,770
General Franky?

471
00:34:04,630 --> 00:34:05,460
What?

472
00:34:05,543 --> 00:34:06,803
So we have to take him?

473
00:34:07,010 --> 00:34:08,250
Well, this sucks.

474
00:34:09,030 --> 00:34:10,450
Don't you worry, Nami!

475
00:34:10,730 --> 00:34:12,330
I'm on bodyguard duty.

476
00:34:12,630 --> 00:34:14,042
Oh my, what a gentleman.

477
00:34:14,450 --> 00:34:17,470
Thank you, I feel much
safer now. Uh, what?

478
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:20,007
Shut up and unlock these
shitty shoes already!

479
00:34:20,090 --> 00:34:21,502
I wasn't talking to you!

480
00:34:22,050 --> 00:34:24,787
Oh no! Atlas! This is serious!

481
00:34:24,870 --> 00:34:26,341
She's not pooping at all.

482
00:34:26,750 --> 00:34:28,570
Don't worry, we'll save you.

483
00:34:28,790 --> 00:34:30,849
Ready a repair session immediately.

484
00:34:31,030 --> 00:34:32,030
Patient incoming.

485
00:34:32,230 --> 00:34:33,907
Thank you for bringing her in.

486
00:34:33,990 --> 00:34:35,696
You can leave the rest to us.

487
00:34:36,110 --> 00:34:37,650
Of course. Good luck.

488
00:34:37,910 --> 00:34:39,247
Hey, screws for brains.

489
00:34:39,330 --> 00:34:40,918
Where the hell is Vegapunk?

490
00:34:41,570 --> 00:34:43,450
I know he's in here somewhere.

491
00:34:44,130 --> 00:34:45,110
Tell me now.

492
00:34:45,650 --> 00:34:46,670
Barney, stop it.

493
00:34:47,050 --> 00:34:48,610
You need to calm down.

494
00:34:51,470 --> 00:34:52,447
Wait a sec.

495
00:34:52,530 --> 00:34:54,450
Is this his lab?

496
00:34:55,090 --> 00:34:55,920
Wow!

497
00:34:56,210 --> 00:34:57,410
So cool!

498
00:34:57,990 --> 00:34:59,637
Are you seeing this, Bonnie?

499
00:35:00,830 --> 00:35:02,610
That ancient bastard!

500
00:35:03,190 --> 00:35:04,830
I'm gonna make him pay!

501
00:35:09,110 --> 00:35:09,940
Bonnie!

502
00:35:10,310 --> 00:35:11,839
Wait, where are you going?

503
00:35:15,570 --> 00:35:19,670
I told Vegapunk to turn my father
back to normal, and what did he do?

504
00:35:20,750 --> 00:35:22,670
He sipped bugs on me!

505
00:35:26,930 --> 00:35:28,870
I'm going to bury him for this.

506
00:35:29,390 --> 00:35:30,220
I...

507
00:35:30,303 --> 00:35:32,498
don't think the bugs
were his fault, though.

508
00:35:32,610 --> 00:35:33,440
Ugh...

509
00:35:33,523 --> 00:35:34,353
Sonic, wait!

510
00:35:34,490 --> 00:35:36,019
We need to stick together!

511
00:35:36,230 --> 00:35:37,510
Hey, come back!

512
00:35:51,770 --> 00:35:54,467
Our authority chips are
finally back in effect.

513
00:35:54,550 --> 00:35:56,810
The Seraphim follow our orders now.

514
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:59,471
Who's ready for a little revenge?

515
00:35:59,930 --> 00:36:02,070
I took down one of the satellites.

516
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:06,467
Including Vegapunk himself,
there are six more.

517
00:36:06,550 --> 00:36:08,050
This might not be easy.

518
00:36:08,490 --> 00:36:10,843
That's assuming we can even get to them.

519
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:15,050
Trust me, that defense system
is nothing to scoff at.

520
00:36:17,010 --> 00:36:19,847
We'll see how long it
lasts against our forces.

521
00:36:19,930 --> 00:36:21,647
Lock down the island.

522
00:36:21,730 --> 00:36:23,407
Destroy every last ship.

523
00:36:23,490 --> 00:36:26,067
You can find no one escapes.

524
00:36:26,150 --> 00:36:27,450
Egghead on our watch.

525
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:41,707
The Straw Hats are protecting vagabond.

526
00:36:41,790 --> 00:36:43,167
How nice of them.

527
00:36:43,250 --> 00:36:46,930
Well, I'm sure they'll be a big help.

528
00:36:49,330 --> 00:36:52,130
Too bad they still won't escape.

529
00:36:55,670 --> 00:36:59,050
They're in for one hell
of a surprise, after all.

530
00:37:00,990 --> 00:37:04,150
All right, proceed
according to plan, boys.

531
00:37:04,850 --> 00:37:07,410
Send every last ship we have...

532
00:37:09,110 --> 00:37:11,030
to Egghead Island.

533
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:51,890
Thank you.
